(GRM Discrepancy 2 - minimal repro. primary's fourth alternative, `"("
 expr ")"` (:5231), claims parentheses group expressions. They do not -
 parentheses are Vox's comment delimiters (LANGUAGE.md documents this
 elsewhere), so `(2 add 3)` is read as a comment and the statement loses
 its value entirely. Cross-ref EXP-D5 (expressions.md), which found this
 first, with the identical pro-compiler reading: the comment syntax is
 documented and load-bearing everywhere else in the language, `{...}` is
 the actual documented grouping punctuation (:1826, 1832), and the
 Grammar Summary's `"(" expr ")"` line is a leftover from an EBNF
 template, not a claim anyone verified against the implementation.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D2.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   error: Expected a statement, got Period
   (no binary produced; compile error)
)
a number called n is (2 add 3).
Print n.
